% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `essential_scrolling_menu`,
% compiled by psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS:
% the class is lost (docs/simpos/subsystems/window.md §0.3, §1.6, the
% scrolling menus).  MENDELS (IFS No.61), 2026-11-27: the variable editor
% of its method editor (med_win.esp:40-45, 213-218), made with
% nature([with_superior_input_buffer, with_shared_window]) (TM-125's
% create option that adds classes; not acted on here: basic_window.esp's
% head) and placed inside the `base` later.
%
% THE NATURE LIST IS INFERENCE: that of
% essential_scrolling_menu_with_superior_input_buffer.esp (whose head
% has the sources) without with_superior_input_buffer, which the name
% leaves out.  It has no method of its own.

class essential_scrolling_menu has

nature
        labeled_sash,
        as_scrolling_menu,
        as_single_select,
        as_mouse_input,
        inferior_window;

end.
